; pictures' formats decoded, the three born of the web or for it: PNG
; (Png: made on the net in 1995 to replace GIF, the W3C's own),
; SVG (Svg: a drawing read and made pixels) -- both elm-playground's,
; copied to be told here and to grow -- and WebP (Webp: the
; container; Vp8l: the lossless format; Vp8: the lossy one, a frame of
; the VP8 video codec). The older formats (GIF, JPEG) came to the web
; from outside and stay elm-playground's. Pure OCaml, bytes in and
; pixels out.
;
; Wrapped, as Images (and as libs/network is, for the same reason):
; the Playground itself reads and writes PNG (a texture, a frame
; dumped) with tiny_libs' Png, and two modules Png in one program
; would not link. Never written, though: the libraries using it say
; (flags (:standard -open Images)), and their code Png.decode,
; Webp.decode, ours.
(library
 (name images)
 (wrapped true)
 (libraries
   tiny_libs.graphics_rgba ; Rgba_image: the pixels given back
   mini_dom lang_xml ; Dom, Xml: a drawing is a document, an SVG file read
   tiny_libs.compression ; Huffman: WebP's prefix codes; Inflate, Deflate: PNG's pixels
   ; Svg's: polygons filled and stroked (Fill, Stroke, Framebuffer),
   ; curves made lines and transforms composed (Curve, Affine)
   tiny_libs.graphics_core tiny_libs.graphics_2d tiny_libs.graphics_2d_geometry))
